course: dictionary
lesson: 4846
title: Hygiene: keeping clean to stay healthy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hygiene means keeping yourself and the things around you clean, so that germs do not spread and make people ill. Germs are tiny living things that can make you sick. Good hygiene is what you do to stop them.
explain: The word sounds grand, but the idea is simple. Washing your hands with soap after the toilet and before you eat is hand hygiene. Brushing your teeth is dental hygiene. Keeping a kitchen and food clean is food hygiene.
explain: The context gives you the meaning. «Zoos ask visitors not to pick up feathers, for hygiene.» The words "for hygiene" tell you the reason is cleanliness and health. Ask yourself what word would fit: clean and healthy care fits best.
explain: A long, official name can hide a simple idea. A shop sign says «feminine hygiene products», and the long words just mean a product for personal cleanliness. When a word is hard, try swapping in a simpler one and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Hygiene means keeping clean to stay healthy and to stop germs spreading.
fact: Hand hygiene means washing your hands with soap, especially after the toilet and before eating.
fact: Dental hygiene means brushing and looking after your teeth.
fact: Hygiene is an uncountable noun, so we say «good hygiene», not «a hygiene».
fact: «Zoos ask visitors not to pick up feathers, for hygiene» because keeping clean helps stop germs spreading.
exercise: «Good hygiene stops germs from spreading.» What does hygiene mean? | Wearing bright clothes every day | Eating sweets slowly | Keeping your bedroom tidy for fun | *Keeping yourself and things around you clean to stay healthy
exercise: Which example shows hand hygiene? | Going to bed late | Sharing your drink with a friend | Painting your fingernails | *Washing your hands with soap after the toilet
exercise: «Zoos ask visitors not to pick up feathers, for hygiene.» Why do they ask this? | To make the path look bigger | To help the birds fly faster | *To keep clean and stop germs spreading | To take the feathers home as souvenirs
test: Which word means keeping clean to stay healthy? | Moult | *Hygiene | Permit | Feather
test: Which phrase means looking after your teeth? | *Dental hygiene | Zoo hygiene | Food hygiene | Hand hygiene
exam: Why is good hygiene important? | *To stop germs spreading and keep people healthy | To make your hair shine | To help you grow taller faster | To stop birds losing their feathers
